    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it (along with the full `mvn test` build) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature end-to-end, keeping each concern in its own small unit.\n\n**What the feature does:** When `POST /api/owners` is called with `sharesHousehold: true` and the new owner matches an existing owner's household (same last name + address, compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace), creation is allowed and the new owner plus every existing household member are stamped with the same stable `householdId`, which is now returned on `GET`. Without the flag, a matching household is still rejected with `DuplicateHouseholdException` as before.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `household_id` column mapping with getter/setter (and to `toString`).\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_id` column.\n- **`validation/HouseholdKey.java`** (new) \u2014 single-responsibility component that computes an owner's canonical household key (normalized last name + address). Normalization logic now lives here once.\n- **`validation/HouseholdDuplicateValidator.java`** \u2014 refactored to delegate to `HouseholdKey` (no duplicated normalization) and to expose `findHouseholdMembers(...)`, with `sharesHouseholdWithExisting(...)` kept as a thin wrapper.\n- **`validation/HouseholdIdGenerator.java`** (new) \u2014 derives the stable shared id deterministically from the `HouseholdKey` (`HH-` + 16 hex chars of SHA-256), so all members of a household map to the same value regardless of creation order.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `rejectDuplicateHousehold` with `applyHouseholdPolicy`, which finds household members once, rejects when not opted in, and otherwise stamps the new owner and any un-stamped existing members with the shared id.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignore `householdId` on the `OwnerFields \u2192 Owner` mapping (it's not a client-editable field); it maps automatically on `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto`.\n\nThe `householdId` derivation being deterministic makes it a genuinely stable shared identifier and keeps `b`/`c` (and the original member) consistent no matter the join order.",
